# trait_mixin.tkr — §9.4 trait-mixin (self-contained concrete mixin, flattened into a composer, and
# traits-compose-traits), exercised end to end on the host build. Each row addresses its scenario BY
# NAME: `main.tks` asserts the scenario's announced value with `teko::assert::eq_i64` and prints
# `scenario <name>: ok`, the line the row below demands. The same program runs through the native
# lowering and the C lowering; a divergence in either backend fails its row.

Feature: trait_mixin — a trait is a self-contained concrete mixin flattened into a composer (§9.4)

  Scenario: flatten_self_host — a trait field + a method reading it, flattened, self resolving to the host
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario flatten_self_host: ok"

  Scenario: static_factory — a `static fn` factory returning `self` (the composing host)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario static_factory: ok"

  Scenario: diamond_absorb — one trait reached by two composition paths is absorbed once (idempotent)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario diamond_absorb: ok"

  Scenario: compose_trait — trait-composes-trait, a method calling `self.v()` of the composed trait
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario compose_trait: ok"

  Scenario: service_compose — a trait flattened into a `service` host, resolved via svc<>
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario service_compose: ok"
